Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient with mocked fetch

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock global fetch (no real network calls), covering URL/header construction, successful parsing, HTTP errors, missing key errors, parse errors, private apiKey, mock mode behavior, and strict opt-in guarantees.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts contains vitest tests using mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) with afterEach restoration, covering: (a) correct RapidAPI URL and header construction, (b) successful response parsed into FlightResult[], (c) HTTP 4xx rejection with status code in error message, (d) missing API key constructor error, (e) malformed response body rejects with parse/validation error
- Test verifies apiKey is stored as private field (not publicly readable), empty-string apiKey and empty-string RAPIDAPI_KEY both throw missing-key Error, and constructor-provided apiKey takes precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY env var
- Test verifies HTTP error messages do not include the apiKey value anywhere in the error string
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture FlightResult[] (≥2 results, valid shape, varying prices) without any fetch invocation (spy asserts never called)
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API with non-'true' values ('false', '1', 'TRUE', empty string, unset) performs real fetch call — strict opt-in, not fuzzy truthy
- Test verifies real API failures (4xx, 5xx, network error, malformed body) are never silently replaced with mock/fixture data — mock mode only activates via explicit env var, never as automatic fallback
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class SkyscannerClient has private field #apiKey storing the API key
- Constructor signature: constructor(options: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message 'Missing API key: provide apiKey option or set RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable' when apiKey option is undefined/null/empty AND RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is undefined/null/empty
- Constructor prioritizes options.apiKey over process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY when both provided
- Method searchFlights signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env var check: process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string comparison, not truthy)
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', returns hardcoded array of 3 FlightResult objects with prices 299, 450, 199
- Mock data airlines: 'MockAir', 'MockAir Plus', 'BudgetMock'
- Mock data currencies: all 'USD'
- Mock data stops: 0, 1, 2 (varying values)
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API !== 'true', performs real fetch to 'https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v3/flights/live/search/create'
- Fetch headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with #apiKey value, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com'
- Query params set: origin, destination, date (always); adults (only if defined)
- On HTTP error (!response.ok), throws Error with message `HTTP error: ${response.status}`
- HTTP error message does NOT include apiKey value
- Response parsing: checks data.results first, then data.data, defaults to empty array
- Validates response is array: throws Error 'Invalid response: expected results array' if not array
- Validates each item is object: throws Error 'Invalid response: result item is not an object' if not object
- Validates required fields: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- On validation failure throws Error 'Invalid response: missing or malformed required fields'
- No validation on adults lower bound (adults=0 is valid)
- No validation on adults upper bound
- No validation on date format
- No validation on origin/destination format (IATA codes)
- No retry logic on fetch failure
- No timeout configuration on fetch

## Mock Strategy
